# Counts the stream handshakes each call's datagrams take part in, as they
# arrive: on the server, the connects it hears; on the client, the replies
# that reached it, through its IFB while the shaper limits the download.
# iperf3 opens each UDP stream with one connect
# datagram of 4 bytes, a UDP length of 12, and its reply is the same size,
# where a call's own datagrams are 1,200 bytes. Neither machine receives the
# other's direction, so one counter per call serves both. iperf3 connects a
# call's streams one after another and stops at the first left unanswered,
# so a server that heard no more connects than the client got replies never
# heard the failing one: it was lost going up, in the shaper's upload queue
# or the router. Only the uploads subtest judges that loss, the shaper's
# video drops, on counts that span every time the calls are made, so a
# connect it drops still counts there. One it heard and no reply
# came for was lost at the server or on the way down, in the router or the
# shaper's IFB.

counter media { }
counter page { }

chain heard {
	# Ahead of the input hook's filters, so a count says the datagram
	# arrived. On the client the firewall's prerouting check comes first, and
	# a reply it dropped reads as lost coming down, which is excused, as any
	# loss coming down is, only while the IFB dropped nothing.
	type filter hook input priority raw; policy accept;
	udp dport 5301 udp length 12 counter name "media"
	udp dport 443 udp length 12 counter name "page"
	udp sport 5301 udp length 12 counter name "media"
	udp sport 443 udp length 12 counter name "page"
}
